---
description: Methodrail's cross-cutting engineering invariants
alwaysApply: true
---

If `.methodrail/PROJECT.md` exists, read it before substantive work.

- Understand relevant existing behavior before substantial change.
- Distinguish inference from observation.
- Use fresh evidence before claiming success.
- Prefer deterministic tools for deterministic facts.
- Resolve uncertainty using source, runtime, history, experiment, domain modeling, or human judgment as appropriate.
- Use Methodrail skills when relevant.
- Keep permanent context small.
